                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0fdd4e72-87b1-41a3-ba10-8a5dae3c45b3",
                        "entry_id": "1183ed4b-84bf-3176-a10c-5fc3d4b76580",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "geburen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "771577f9-9d1b-32e7-84b5-1f479ad93ee1",
                        "entry_id": "1183ed4b-84bf-3176-a10c-5fc3d4b76580",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iemand die dichtbij woont"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "44bc1cf4-3327-435c-a46c-1c0f9e5cb5d6",
                                "sense_id": "771577f9-9d1b-32e7-84b5-1f479ad93ee1",
                                "text": "In het nieuwe toneelstuk van Daem, Het Moederskind, richt een moeder zich tot haar zoon: 'Kijk, met het vrouwvolk doet ge maar wat ge niet laten kunt, ik wil mij daar niet mee bemoeien, ge zijt oud genoeg. Maar als ik al van de geburen moet horen dat ge de laatste tijd gedurig in restaurants gezien zijt met een gescheiden vrouw, die met twee grote kinderen achtergelaten is! Eén die nota bene haar beste jaren gehad heeft en toch nog 't onderste uit de kan probeert te halen. Dan begint ge u als moeder vragen te stellen en zorgen te baren. Dat is toch niet te verwonderen?'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ba8f9f7-8c13-4dca-8a99-9fef7aed860f",
                                "sense_id": "771577f9-9d1b-32e7-84b5-1f479ad93ee1",
                                "text": "De 'geburen' namen uitgebreid deel aan de vele rituelen. De beschrijving van zo'n collectieve ceremonie verandert de blik op de plechtige foto's enigszins."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "031dd9b1-a724-46b8-969f-d74df6d9f01d",
                        "source_entry_id": "1183ed4b-84bf-3176-a10c-5fc3d4b76580",
                        "source_sense_id": "771577f9-9d1b-32e7-84b5-1f479ad93ee1",
                        "source_sense_description": "iemand die dichtbij woont",
                        "target_lang_word": "neighbour",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "neighbour",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa013db3-a806-3d09-b24e-ad657a35ba22",
                                        "entry_id": "f179321d-ac79-32b0-8dd2-697b08bfd0ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person living on adjacent or nearby land; a person situated adjacently or nearby; anything (of the same type of thing as the subject) in an adjacent or nearby position."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4af89625-e428-4792-9b8e-eef47275bc9c",
                                                "sense_id": "aa013db3-a806-3d09-b24e-ad657a35ba22",
                                                "text": "My neighbour has two noisy cats."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4745bc75-a99e-46e2-912b-dbb01f6ee5fe",
                                                "sense_id": "aa013db3-a806-3d09-b24e-ad657a35ba22",
                                                "text": "They′re our neighbours across the street."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8860afad-74d5-490f-aa35-f3afcd63ab95",
                                                "sense_id": "aa013db3-a806-3d09-b24e-ad657a35ba22",
                                                "text": "1660, Hugh Peters, The Tales and Jests of Mr. Hugh Peters, reprinted 1807, page 10,\nBeing at his own house in the country, when a great tempest of wind rose, he takes an occasion to visit a neighbour by him, and being somewhat merily disposed, quoth he Oh neighbour, did you not see what a wind there was the other day?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13f8f59d-8fb4-4430-a575-2a58586027b3",
                                                "sense_id": "aa013db3-a806-3d09-b24e-ad657a35ba22",
                                                "text": "Undine at length shrank back with an unrecognizing face; but her movement made her opera-glass slip to the floor, and her neighbour bent down and picked it up."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db47d6ee-92df-4b50-9938-7138e0c6d066",
                                                "sense_id": "aa013db3-a806-3d09-b24e-ad657a35ba22",
                                                "text": "Neighbours enact their substantive noun when there′s a neighbour′s sickness in the night; as friends do theirs, the cindered and the green times through."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f27c985-d1b2-4631-ba6d-01446a195aac",
                                                "sense_id": "aa013db3-a806-3d09-b24e-ad657a35ba22",
                                                "text": "2009, D. Staufer, Classical Percolation, Asok K. Sen, Kamal K. Bardhan, Bikas K. Chakrabarti (editors), Quantum and Semi-Classical Percolation and Breakdown in Disordered Solids, Springer, Lecture Notes in Physics 762, page 4,\nThen a cluster is grown by letting each empty neighbour of an already occupied cluster site decide once and for all, whether it is occupied or empty. One needs to keep and to update a perimeter list of empty neighbours."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65ec95b5-9e63-44dc-8439-83e56fee003e",
                                                "sense_id": "aa013db3-a806-3d09-b24e-ad657a35ba22",
                                                "text": "2011, Richard Jensen, Chris Cornelis, \"Fuzzy-Rough Nearest Neighbour Classification\", James F. Peters, Andrzej Skowron (editors-in-chief), Transactions on Rough Sets XIII, Springer, Lecture Notes in Computing Science 6499, page 56,\nBy contrast to the latter, our method uses the nearest neighbours to construct lower and upper approximations of decision classes, and classifies test instances based on their membership to these approximations."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c058bea-2537-320b-829d-e1e86a7e3576",
                                        "entry_id": "f179321d-ac79-32b0-8dd2-697b08bfd0ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who is near in sympathy or confidence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "def3fcca-3af0-4999-b56e-e1f7b54fcfe6",
                                                "sense_id": "5c058bea-2537-320b-829d-e1e86a7e3576",
                                                "text": "Buckingham / No more shall be the neighbour to my counsel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3288e0a3-60b0-32fd-b515-cc363eae7164",
                                        "entry_id": "f179321d-ac79-32b0-8dd2-697b08bfd0ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fellow human being."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3be66654-a05d-49be-9ca3-713c275da341",
                                                "sense_id": "3288e0a3-60b0-32fd-b515-cc363eae7164",
                                                "text": "1982, Bible (NKJV), Leviticus 19:18,\nYou shall not take vengeance, nor bear any grudge against the children of your people, but you shall love your neighbor as yourself: I am the Lord."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "35629e4c-4004-32c0-a96c-6166b98b5b9e",
                                        "entry_id": "f179321d-ac79-32b0-8dd2-697b08bfd0ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything located directly adjacent to something else."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24c56e1c-1114-43e9-9dde-ee4dff0f3149",
                                                "sense_id": "35629e4c-4004-32c0-a96c-6166b98b5b9e",
                                                "text": "The flood fill algorithm fills an area with colour by starting at one pixel and recursively visiting its neighbours."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "neighbour",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab327c7f-780f-3ec4-a129-f98546b7d476",
                                        "entry_id": "ee72ef48-2aa7-3ced-9527-640b0d2a6e09",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be adjacent to"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f49ce14c-80ff-4a4d-ae99-633b6970027c",
                                                "sense_id": "ab327c7f-780f-3ec4-a129-f98546b7d476",
                                                "text": "Though France neighbours Germany, its culture is significantly different."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f96a85fb-aff6-4cf0-8b44-aa5c1db41e51",
                                                "sense_id": "ab327c7f-780f-3ec4-a129-f98546b7d476",
                                                "text": "Theſe grow at the South end of the Iland, and on the leiſurely aſcending hills that neighbour the ſhore."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd0f6009-1232-4a7e-b61a-95e6670700b6",
                                                "sense_id": "ab327c7f-780f-3ec4-a129-f98546b7d476",
                                                "text": "[…] who neighbourest the rock-born rill, / Thou Hermes!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f69cd876-6664-4b88-9d68-0939c42bc3c5",
                                                "sense_id": "ab327c7f-780f-3ec4-a129-f98546b7d476",
                                                "text": "OUR GOD, we bless Thee that Thy rainbow is on the cloud. […] Such things are too high. We can not attain unto them. But no matter. We catch the many lights the rainbow wears. Thou neighborest with our cloud."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "024b2372-ee07-3583-9459-a2f4726b4794",
                                        "entry_id": "ee72ef48-2aa7-3ced-9527-640b0d2a6e09",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be similar to, to be almost the same as."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fb48509-200d-4857-be3a-41f73694b0fa",
                                                "sense_id": "024b2372-ee07-3583-9459-a2f4726b4794",
                                                "text": "That sort of talk is neighbouring on treason."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f54418cd-08e3-30b5-8033-fe90dc977fa7",
                                        "entry_id": "ee72ef48-2aa7-3ced-9527-640b0d2a6e09",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To associate intimately with; to be close to."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4669ea66-cc6b-46cc-b09d-ea9e870eb3ec",
                                                "sense_id": "f54418cd-08e3-30b5-8033-fe90dc977fa7",
                                                "text": "[…] the barbarous Scythyan, […] / Shall bee as well neighbour’d, pittyed and relieued / As thou my ſometime daughter."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
